# Signing for the corpse device tests. Copy to signing.env and fill in.
# signing.env is gitignored: it names your team and profiles, which are yours.
#
# Find the values with:
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
#   ls ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/UserData/Provisioning\ Profiles/
#
# The host and the extension each need a profile carrying the App Group, which
# Xcode creates the first time you set the team on those targets with automatic
# signing. After that these tests run from a terminal with Xcode closed.

# Your team identifier.
TUIST_CORPSE_TEAM=

# Only the team is needed. Signing is automatic and the run script passes
# -allowProvisioningUpdates, so Xcode's own managed profiles are used and
# refreshed without Xcode being open.

# Optional: pin a device instead of taking the first connected one.
# CORPSE_DEVICE_ID=
